ns; identical auctions reuse physical games. Intervals are descriptive and unadjusted for repeated monitoring.","feed":{"published_epoch":1794553556.1574068,"interval_seconds":60,"next_update_epoch":1794553616.1574068},"model_note":"Gen 9 (9a-32) is the Gen 8 prototype (8p-32: Gen 7.1 standard with the play read from trick 1 at exponent 1.0, policy v4.1) reading each partnership through a player model: house bots are modelled as the house system, so the auction is read by replaying the house bidder after the opening lead; BEN and anyone without a model are read exactly as 8p-32 reads them. It plays a random one of its exactly equal-best cards (exploration 1.0). No experience is carried: the models are what each side declares. 8p-32 is the control. 8s-32 and 71s-32 are the arena's Gen 8 and Gen 7.1 (same identities). docs/gen9/cohort.md.","source_cohort_overlap":false,"allocation":{"9a-32~8s-32":1,"9a-32~71s-32":1,"9a-32~8p-32":1},"statistics_policy":{},"collection":{"updated_epoch":1794553547.198209,"running":true,"workers":8,"total_completed":70,"training_only_completed":0},"difference_views":{"0":{"groups":{"9a-32~8s-32":{"bidding":{"n":24,"total":0,"mean":0.0,"variance":0.0,"sd":0.0,"se":0.0,"ci":[0.0,0.0],"wins":0,"ties":24,"losses":0},"play":{"n":24,"total":14,"mean":0.5833333333333334,"variance":18.079710144927535,"sd":4.252024240867817,"se":0.8679408136725957,"ci":[-1.2121390362637832,2.3788057029304497],"wins":5,"ties":17,"losses":2},"total":{"n":24,"total":14,"mean":0.5833333333333334,"variance":18.079710144927535,"sd":4.252024240867817,"se":0.8679408136725957,"ci":[-1.2121390362637832,2.3788057029304497],"wins":5,"ties":17,"losses":2},"different_bidding":0},"9a-32~71s-32":{"bidding":{"n":23,"total":0,"mean":0.0,"variance":0.0,"sd":0.0,"se":0.0,"ci":[0.0,0.0],"wins":0,"ties":23,"losses":0},"play":{"n":23,"total":52,"mean":2.260869565217391,"variance":25.11067193675889,"sd":5.011054972434336,"se":1.0448771913849366,"ci":[0.09392689873697124,4.427812231697811